  "term": "mathematical psychology",
  "definition": "Mathematical psychology is an approach to psychology that uses mathematical equations and analysis to model behavior. In this source, it refers to developing and studying formal models of operant-control behavior, including probabilistic solutions and theoretical tools such as fixed point methods.",
